Z||000009||Gerald||10-25-2001||12:56 PM||||From what I've come to understand in all my readings is that any 88 GT/Formula is ready for the swap. The rack and pinion is read to accept the electric pump because all the fittings are already on it. The pump it self is actually being used on a GM car now!!!!<BR>The EV1 as you all know has no engine so the pump that was gonna be used for the Fiero is being used on that car. I doubt its cheap thou   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P> I also really want to get that 16 valve in my car. I think the steering is fine as it is.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gerald (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000010||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||01:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87V6GT:<BR><B>Where can I get the power steering unit for my GT?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...The power steering unit shown above was never actually sold on any production cars.  I've heard (rumor?) that Rodney Dickman acquired one of the power assist units and has it installed on one of his cars.  Other than that there have been others who have adapted other powersteering (full-time) units to their Fiero.  Supposedly the Merkur XR4Ti Power steering unit was a "bolt" on for the Fiero... just need to add a PS pump!  Other theories have come up with a Volvo (not sure of model) unit being used- this possibility stemed from AUS using a Volvo Rack & Pinion in his Australian Right hand drive conversion (which I'd still love to buy... AUS?).  Hope this answers your basic question- or at least gives a direction to run with.  Also, search the Technical section... there was someone there that had lots of info (they had one in their car!) think is was Kasdan?  Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfiero||10-25-2001||02:15 PM||||Screw the SD4 and the power steering.......I want those '88 GT tan leather seats!!!  <P>That's one option that I want on my 16K mile '88 GT.......I'll pay a finders fee for anyone who can locate a low mileage set of these for me (must be from a low mileage '88 GT.....i.e. less than 16K miles).  I am serious! I would trade my 16K mile (MINT) cloth seats <B>plus</B> an obscene amount of cash for a perfect set of factory beechwood leather seats.  Anyone? <P><BR>BTW....Rodney does have an original power steering rack, but I do not believe he has installed it on his Fiero.  If I remember correctly, he has a Link power steering unit that uses a Merkur XR4Ti rack.<BR>||||reg||10
