Z||000015||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||04:15 PM||||Yes, pontiac did make the superduty 4cyl engine... it was used in the actual indy pacecar, as well as in racing applications.  No, they were not available in any production vehicle- just special order from GM.  Someone here in Minn has one, and is installing it in his 84 Indy... it's about half finished through a multi-year project.  Heard something about heading to Utah when it's finished...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||Brandon86SE||10-25-2001||04:18 PM||||I did a little bit of research on the engine, and found that it is a GM racing engine.  The parts to build it are available from your GM dealership.<P>Total cost would be around $12000US.<BR>Bore - 4.00" - 4.125"<BR>Stroke - 3.1" - 3.625"<BR>Hemi chambers<BR>DOHC<BR>DOHV (16V)<BR>HP - 370-400+ depending on bore and stroke<BR>TQ - 340+ depending on bore and stroke<P>This is very interesting to me, and I did find this information on a Fiero site, wondering if anyone's done it?????????  I know that I would be interested. (once I'm out of college and have money)  I'd rather put $12000 into that than a lambo body kit for example.  And the best thing is that it is only a 3.0L, which would leave plenty of room for TT's, or SC.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.  I have lots of concrete future mod plans, but engine is the one thing still up in the air.<P>Oh, the site I found this is the <A HREF="http://w1.859.telia.com/~u85904231/users/fieroclub/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Swedish Fiero Club</A> site.  Check under engines, couldn't link directly.<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000017||Brandon86SE||10-25-2001||05:54 PM||||Hey Minn, sounds sweet, any chance of them making a swing to Calgary on that trip to Utah?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  That's a car I'd like to see!  I'm quite interested on how this turns out for him (her?), keep us posted.<P>Brandon||||reg||10
Z||000018||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||06:37 PM||||Not sure if he's doing it top secret or what...? Oh well.  Just a long-term project.  <B>He</B> is the current VP of the <B>Minnesota Fieros Forever</B> club... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mn.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mn.org</A>   if you can't figure out who it is from the first page you see, then you probably don't need to know!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||Master_Sushi||10-25-2001||07:02 PM||||I'll take an 88GT with the Superduty,Power Steering, and the beachwood seats!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>A fiero with all three of those items *would* have been a world class sports car, if not supercar!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">WHAT WAS GM THINKING WHAT THEY KILLED THEM?!!?!?!? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||11
