Z||000021||Earl||10-26-2001||04:06 AM||||I dont know nothing bout no power stering <BR>My arms are big enough to turn my 84 se with a 10 inch steering wheel .<BR>How ever if anyone is interested GM produces a 3.0 L 4cyl for mercruiser its rated at 140 hp stock with non cross flow head the marine block is suposed to be verry close to the super duty or so I am led to belive .The only snag is the transmition bolt patern is the same as the SBC so an adapter plate is nessasary I am looking in to building one for myself .<BR> Kansas Racing products produces the super duty engine for the lincoln truck series however I cant see spending $25,000 on any motor their web site is linked off of fiero secreats web site (I think) ||||reg||1
Z||000022||tomcat06085||10-26-2001||07:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gerald:<BR><B>From what I've come to understand in all my readings is that any 88 GT/Formula is ready for the swap. The rack and pinion is read to accept the electric pump because all the fittings are already on it. The pump it self is actually being used on a GM car now!!!!<BR>The EV1 as you all know has no engine so the pump that was gonna be used for the Fiero is being used on that car. I doubt its cheap thou    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P> I also really want to get that 16 valve in my car. I think the steering is fine as it is.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>[This message has been edited by Gerald (edited 10-25-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gerald...do you have any links or liturature about the rack being ready as it is...I just got an 88GT and intend to put power steering in it one way or the other. My son is going to do the work...he said he's seen adaptations on other GM cars, but we don't have concrete stuff yet, like part numbers, models that used the same front end parts, all the fine points...it would save him a lot of trial and error.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://jrreeves.com/images/blckfire.jpg"> <BR>tomcat...Thanks for the help!||||reg||5
